// ### 2. Why does this throw a `ReferenceError`?

// ```js
// sayHello();

// const sayHello = function () {
//     console.log("Hello");
// };
// ```

// **Answer:**

// ```text
// ReferenceError
// ```

// `const` creates the binding during environment setup, but it remains **uninitialized** until execution reaches the declaration.

// Accessing it during this period means accessing a variable in the **Temporal Dead Zone (TDZ)**.

